tool_definitions.description:
Check stock: Use this to check available quantity and reorder point for a product by name or SKU. Do not use this tool for changing stock or placing an order. Inputs include a readable customer or product name when relevant; output labels are designed for a user to recognize the matching record. Errors identify a field and safe next step. Results are bounded, and continuation metadata is included when more results exist.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__good_a__check_stock(args: {
  // Product name or SKU, e.g. Harju 80 sauna heater
  product: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Find account: Use this to resolve a customer from its legal or trading name and view its account status. Do not use this tool for searching invoices or changing an account. Inputs include a readable customer or product name when relevant; output labels are designed for a user to recognize the matching record. Errors identify a field and safe next step. Results are bounded, and continuation metadata is included when more results exist.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__good_a__find_account(args: {
  // Customer legal or trading name, e.g. Kelo Hotels Oy
  name: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Place reviewed order: Use this only after the user has reviewed a preview and explicitly asked to place it. Do not use this tool for drafting, editing, or cancelling an order. Inputs include a readable customer or product name when relevant; output labels are designed for a user to recognize the matching record. Errors identify a field and safe next step. Results are bounded, and continuation metadata is included when more results exist.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__good_a__place_order(args: {
  // Required confirmation value after the user approves this exact preview
  confirmation: "CONFIRM";
  // Client-generated key reused for an exact retry, at least 8 characters
  idempotencyKey: string;
  // Preview ID returned by preview_order, e.g. PREVIEW-...
  previewId: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Preview order: Use this to calculate a draft order and review its customer, items, and total before placement. Do not use this tool for placing or cancelling an order. Inputs include a readable customer or product name when relevant; output labels are designed for a user to recognize the matching record. Errors identify a field and safe next step. Results are bounded, and continuation metadata is included when more results exist.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__good_a__preview_order(args: {
  // Customer legal or trading name, e.g. Kelo Hotels Oy
  customer: string;
  // Whole-unit quantity from 1 to 50
  quantity: number;
  // Product SKU, e.g. HARJU-80
  sku: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Search invoices: Use this to find invoices by readable number, customer name, or payment status. Do not use this tool for creating, sending, or paying an invoice. Inputs include a readable customer or product name when relevant; output labels are designed for a user to recognize the matching record. Errors identify a field and safe next step. Results are bounded, and continuation metadata is included when more results exist.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__good_a__search_invoices(args: {
  // Continuation cursor returned by a previous page
  cursor?: string;
  // Page size from 1 to 50
  limit?: number;
  // Readable invoice number or customer name
  query?: string;
  // Payment state to filter by
  status?: "paid" | "unpaid" | "overdue";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Search orders: Use this to find order status by order number, customer name, or date range. Do not use this tool for creating, changing, or cancelling an order. Inputs include a readable customer or product name when relevant; output labels are designed for a user to recognize the matching record. Errors identify a field and safe next step. Results are bounded, and continuation metadata is included when more results exist.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__good_a__search_orders(args: {
  // Continuation cursor returned by a previous page
  cursor?: string;
  // Inclusive start date in YYYY-MM-DD format, e.g. 2026-10-01
  fromDate?: string;
  // Page size from 1 to 50
  limit?: number;
  // Readable order number or customer name; omit to list recent orders
  query?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

